{{- /* 
    titles.tmpl ~ Titles are important template.
*/ -}}
{{- define "content" }}
<div class="index-intro-section">
  <p class="lead">
    Titles are important, but <em>bad titles make it hard to dupe check uploads and search</em>.
  </p>
  <p class="mb-0">
    <strong class="text-primary">
      The current site policy is to <u>keep titles simple</u>, concise and clean.<br>
      Game titles should match the publisher's official name.
    </strong>
  </p>
</div>

<h4 class="index-section-header">❌ Bad examples:</h4>
<div class="index-intro-section">
  <ol>
    <li><q>Microsoft Visual Studio for WinNT V1.1001.1</q></li>
    <li><q>INC cracktro for EA's Sim City 2000!</q></li>
    <li><q>Zool 2 by Virgin Interactive +16 MEGA trainer</q></li>
    <li><q>Microsoft Windows 95 4.00.950 *STORE RELEASE FINAL*</q></li>
    <li><q>EA NFL 98 100% BYTE PATCHED AND WORKING</q></li>
  </ol>
</div>

<h4 class="index-section-header">✅ Good examples:</h4>
<div class="index-intro-section">
  <ol>
    <li><q>Visual Studio v1.1</q></li>
    <li><q>SimCity 2000</q></li>
    <li><q>Zool 2</q></li>
    <li><q>Windows 95</q></li>
    <li><q>NFL 98 fix</q></li>
  </ol>
</div>

<h4 class="index-section-header">Why not copy and paste?</h4>
<div class="index-intro-section">
  <p class="text-muted small mb-2"><em>Why not copy and paste from the NFO, file_diz.diz, or the directory path?</em></p>
  <p>
  It is common for Scene releases to use mismatched details, bad spellings, and lazy acronyms.
  These make it difficult to run searches for software and game names.
  </p>
  <p>
    For example, this <a href="/f/aa1d41e">release</a> for <em>The Adventures of Tintin : Prisoners of the Sun</em>.<br>
    Uses <em>TINTIN (c) INFOGRAMES</em> for the DIZ, and the title <em>Spirou (c) Infogrames</em> for the NFO.
  </p>
  <p>This <a href="/f/ae273de">release</a> for <q>Jack&nbsp;Nicklaus 4</q> addon uses the meaningless <em><mark>JNG</mark> 4</em> in the DIZ, 
    and has multiple typos in the NFO, <em>Jack <mark>Nick<u>a</u>laus <strike>Golf</strike></mark> 4</em>. 
  </p>
</div>

<h4 class="index-section-header">Naming guide:</h4>
<div class="index-intro-section">
  <ul class="list-group list-group-flush">
    <li class="list-group-item">
      List the name of the game or software before any minimal supplementary info.
      <br>
      <small class="text-body-secondary"><mark>SimCity</mark> fix</small>, 
      <small class="text-body-secondary"><mark>SimCity</mark> addon</small>
    </li>
    <li class="list-group-item">It is fine to use an empty title if the other data or the screenshots provide enough context.
        <br><small class="text-body-secondary">These types of files often do not need a title. Art, logos, courier group NFOs, BBS/FTP adverts, etc.</small>
    </li>
    <li class="list-group-item">
      Do not include unnecessary information.
      <br><small class="text-body-secondary">Semantic software versions, build numbers, or release justifications, <q>100% final</q>, <q>US release</q>, <q>multilanguage</q>, etc.
      <br><strike>SimCity 100% final, SimCity US release, SimCity 1.500.001</strike>
      </small>
    </li>
    <li class="list-group-item">
      Do not include too specific or problematic details, instead append <q>fix</q> or <q>addon</q>.
      <br><small class="text-body-secondary">Avoid terms like, <q>cracked</q>, <q>patched</q>, <q>bytecrack</q>, <q>hack</q>, <q>key</q>, <q>keymaker</q>, <q>generator</q>, <q>serial</q>, etc.</small>
    </li>
    <li class="list-group-item">
      Do not include redundant information.
      <br><small class="text-body-secondary">Words such as <q>trainer</q>, <q>cheat</q>, <q>hint</q>, <q>installer</q>, <q>cracktro</q>, <q>docs</q>, <q>documentation</q>, <q>manual</q>, using the group name, etc.
      <br><strike>SimCity trainer, SimCity +4 cheat, SimCity installer, Manual for SimCity, SimCity by Razor</strike></small>
    </li>
    <li class="list-group-item">
      Do not include the publisher as these can attract DMCA bot take downs when shown on search engines.
      <br><small class="text-body-secondary">
      <strike>EA SimCity, Sim City (C) Electronic Arts, SimCity by Maxis, Sega's Sonic</strike>.<br>
      Exceptions are made for titles using generic nouns and verbs.<br>
      For example, <q>Norton Backup</q>, <q>Atari Football</q>.</small>
    </li>
    <li class="list-group-item">Please do not use:
      <ul class="list-group list-group-flush">
        <li class="list-group-item">Elite text, it's silly and cannot be searched:
        <br><small class="text-body-secondary"><q>εLεε7 τεxτ !s ßαd</q></small></li>
        <li class="list-group-item">File names give no context when used as titles:
        <br><small class="text-body-secondary"><q>R-SCTY2K.ZIP</q></small></li>
        <li class="list-group-item">All capitalized text, as it's hard to read:
        <br><small class="text-body-secondary"><q>ALL CAPS IS ANNOYING</q></small></li>
        <li class="list-group-item">Copy and paste FTP site directories, as it's hard to read and are DMCA triggers:
        <br><small class="text-body-secondary"><q>using.a.copy.and.pasted.directory.name.is.also.annoying.to.read</q></small></li>
      </ul>
    </li>
  </ul>
</div>
{{- end}}
